      "sequence_position": 12,
      "problem": "The projection of the intersection between the elliptic paraboloid $5(x+2)^{2}+3(y+3)^{2}=z$ and the plane $z=2$  onto the $xy$-plane is an ellipse. Find the center of this ellipse.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the paraboloid and the plane $z=2$, we substitute $z=2$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+2)^{2}+3(y+3)^{2} & =z \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}+3(y+3)^{2} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{2/5}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{2/3} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse in the $xy$-plane that has its center at $(-2,-3).$",
